# public-writable-field (#14, Fowler "Encapsulate Variable"): a field
# declared under an EXPLICIT 'public' visibility section of a class -- expose
# it through a property instead. Excludes records, 'published' sections
# (auto-generated DFM components), and the implicit/default section. OFF by
# default -- run with public-writable-field.config.json
# ("enabled": ["public-writable-field"]).
# Line 11 'FHidden: Integer' is under 'private' -> not flagged.
!public-writable-field 11
# Line 13 'FFoo: Integer' is under an explicit 'public' section of a class
# -> FLAGGED (emitted at the field's name, line 13).
public-writable-field 13
# Line 15 'FBar: TControl' is under 'published' (auto-generated DFM
# component dump) -> not flagged.
!public-writable-field 15
# Line 19 'FImplicit: Integer' is in the implicit/default section (no
# visibility keyword yet at the top of the class body) -> not flagged.
!public-writable-field 19
# Line 24 'RX: Integer' is under 'public' but the enclosing type is a
# record (TCoord), not a class -- records legitimately expose fields
# -> not flagged.
!public-writable-field 24
